Oh, really?

522
00:23:43,547 --> 00:23:46,092
Well, shall we fight?
I can... okay.

523
00:23:46,133 --> 00:23:49,469
Stop it! Stop it before
someone gets really hurt.

524
00:23:51,013 --> 00:23:54,225
Here, David,
you should just go.

525
00:23:54,267 --> 00:23:56,434
All right.

526
00:23:56,476 --> 00:23:59,605
But... if I ever do
come back from Minsk

527
00:23:59,646 --> 00:24:02,108
well, you'd just better
watch out.

528
00:24:02,149 --> 00:24:04,193
Well, if I ever go to Minsk,
you'd better watch out.

529
00:24:04,235 --> 00:24:05,485
Oh, you're going to Minsk?

530
00:24:05,527 --> 00:24:07,154
Well, I might.

531
00:24:07,196 --> 00:24:08,530
Really?

532
00:24:08,572 --> 00:24:10,657
Well, if you do,
come in the spring.

533
00:24:10,699 --> 00:24:12,118
It's just lovely there.

534
00:24:12,159 --> 00:24:14,203
Okay, well, guys...

535
00:24:14,245 --> 00:24:16,538
Well... good-bye, Phoebe.

536
00:24:16,580 --> 00:24:17,748
Bye.

537
00:24:17,790 --> 00:24:18,832
Hey, what, are
you kidding me?

538
00:24:18,874 --> 00:24:20,709
Right-o, right-o.

539
00:24:20,751 --> 00:24:22,544
Um...

540
00:24:25,005 --> 00:24:26,548
Take good care of her.

541
00:24:29,718 --> 00:24:31,678
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

542
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:35,682
If you want your key back,
I totally understand.

543
00:24:35,724 --> 00:24:38,602
It's never going to
happen again, right?

544
00:24:38,644 --> 00:24:40,313
Right. Never, never, I swear.

545
00:24:42,564 --> 00:24:45,234
Uh... oh, I just want to say,
if you, uh...

546
00:24:45,276 --> 00:24:48,237
if you do ever come to Minsk,
that's my number.

547
00:24:48,279 --> 00:24:51,365
Um... we'll, uh...
we'll party up Vladnik style.

548
00:24:58,038 --> 00:25:02,960
( recorders playing
"Hot Cross Buns" )

549
00:25:07,381 --> 00:25:09,467
Yeah, all right.

550
00:25:09,507 --> 00:25:11,635
Hey, hey, Ross, check it out.

551
00:25:11,677 --> 00:25:14,054
Sandy taught me
"Hot Cross Buns."

552
00:25:14,096 --> 00:25:15,097
Really?

553
00:25:15,139 --> 00:25:17,183
Sounded like "Three Blind Mice."

554
00:25:17,224 --> 00:25:19,059
No, "Three Blind Mice"
goes like this.

555
00:25:19,101 --> 00:25:20,269
I swear to God...

556
00:25:23,772 --> 00:25:25,065
Who's up for puppets?

557
00:25:25,107 --> 00:25:26,608
Me. I'm up for puppets.

558
00:25:27,609 --> 00:25:28,735
Well, please welcome

559
00:25:28,777 --> 00:25:32,698
the Snufflebumps.

560
00:25:32,739 --> 00:25:34,241
Who wants to be Mr. Wigglemunch

561
00:25:34,283 --> 00:25:36,243
and who's going to be
the Grumpus?

562
00:25:36,285 --> 00:25:37,953
ROSS:
Okay, okay...

563
00:25:37,995 --> 00:25:42,082
how exactly is a two-month-old
supposed to appreciate puppets?

564
00:25:42,124 --> 00:25:45,585
Actually, studies have shown
that the movement and colors

565
00:25:45,627 --> 00:25:47,629
help their cerebral development.

566
00:25:47,671 --> 00:25:50,216
The whimsical characters
are just for us.

567
00:25:54,470 --> 00:25:57,348
I want to be Mr. Wigglemunch.

568
00:25:57,390 --> 00:25:59,599
Oh, my God.

569
00:25:59,641 --> 00:26:02,560
Well, I guess we know
who's going to be the Grumpus.

570
00:26:02,602 --> 00:26:04,771
( laughing )

571
00:26:07,900 --> 00:26:09,609
Well, that was kind of rude.

572
00:26:09,651 --> 00:26:11,153
Oh, I'm sorry.

573
00:26:11,195 --> 00:26:14,990
Please apologize to Sandy
and the Snufflebumps for me.

574
00:26:15,032 --> 00:26:17,659
You know,
he was just doing his job.

575
00:26:17,701 --> 00:26:18,827
You know what?

576
00:26:18,869 --> 00:26:20,787
I'm... I'm sorry
I'm the only one

577
00:26:20,829 --> 00:26:23,832
who isn't in love with
"Gary Poppins" out there...

578
00:26:26,835 --> 00:26:29,922
But I-I-I just... I can't, I
can't go through with this.

579
00:26:29,963 --> 00:26:31,673
Come on, Ross.
No. Hey, you
know what?

580
00:26:31,715 --> 00:26:33,800
I'm sorry,
I would never force you

581
00:26:33,842 --> 00:26:36,845
to hire someone you were
this uncomfortable with.

582
00:26:36,887 --> 00:26:38,972
( sighs )

583
00:26:39,014 --> 00:26:41,434
Oh, that's true.

584
00:26:41,475 --> 00:26:43,018
Thank you.

585
00:26:43,060 --> 00:26:44,811
Well, you're the one
who wants to fire him

586
00:26:44,853 --> 00:26:46,313
so you're going to have
to go do it.

587
00:26:46,355 --> 00:26:48,357
( chuckles )

588
00:26:48,399 --> 00:26:51,277
So, you see, Wigglemunch

589
00:26:51,318 --> 00:26:55,114
that's why
it's important to share.

590
00:26:56,907 --> 00:27:00,035
I am learning so
much from you.

591
00:27:04,915 --> 00:27:06,917
Well, I'm off to Tulsa

592
00:27:06,959 --> 00:27:11,422
so if your maitre d' friend
has any funny Oklahoma jokes

593
00:27:11,464 --> 00:27:15,426
tell him to e-mail me at
www.hahanotsomuch.com.

594
00:27:17,344 --> 00:27:18,929
Honey, you can relax.

595
00:27:18,971 --> 00:27:22,600
Last night at work, Jeffrey
told this really sexist joke.

596
00:27:22,640 --> 00:27:24,893
After that,
not so funny anymore.

597
00:27:24,935 --> 00:27:25,936
Really?
Mm-hmm.

598
00:27:25,978 --> 00:27:27,521
See, that's the thing.

599
00:27:27,563 --> 00:27:29,856
You got to keep
it smart, people.

600
00:27:29,898 --> 00:27:32,276
Okay... don't miss that flight.

601
00:27:32,318 --> 00:27:33,444
You know I love you.

602
00:27:33,486 --> 00:27:35,404
I love you, too.

603
00:27:35,446 --> 00:27:38,365
And I like you as a friend.

604
00:27:38,407 --> 00:27:39,408
Right.

605
00:27:39,450 --> 00:27:40,576
See you later.

606
00:27:40,618 --> 00:27:41,619
See ya.

607
00:27:43,912 --> 00:27:45,663
Did that guy
really make that joke?

608
00:27:45,705 --> 00:27:47,249
No, he still kills me.

609
00:27:47,291 --> 00:27:49,918
Last night he had me
laughing so hard

610
00:27:49,960 --> 00:27:52,129
I swear a little pee came out.

611
00:28:00,304 --> 00:28:01,597
Here it goes.

612
00:28:01,639 --> 00:28:03,182
I can't watch.

613
00:28:03,223 --> 00:28:05,267
It's like firing Elmo.

614
00:28:09,229 --> 00:28:10,730
Sandy, hi.

615
00:28:10,772 --> 00:28:12,024
Hi.

616
00:28:12,065 --> 00:28:14,193
We, uh... we kind
of need to talk.

617
00:28:19,323 --> 00:28:21,699
I'm afraid it's...
it's not working out.

618
00:28:23,910 --> 00:28:26,288
Oh...
Yeah, um...

619
00:28:26,330 --> 00:28:29,958
I mean, Rachel and I think
you are great with Emma.

620
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:32,878
Um... we just feel...

621
00:28:32,919 --> 00:28:35,255
RACHEL:
You. You feel.

622
00:28:35,297 --> 00:28:36,965
I...

623
00:28:37,007 --> 00:28:40,010
just feel that the...

624
00:28:40,052 --> 00:28:42,471
the chemistry isn't right.

625
00:28:42,513 --> 00:28:43,681
I'm-I'm sorry.

626
00:28:43,722 --> 00:28:45,098
We're... We're
more than happy

627
00:28:45,140 --> 00:28:47,100
to give you a good
recommendation, and...

628
00:28:47,142 --> 00:28:48,519
No, no, that's okay.

629
00:28:48,561 --> 00:28:51,271
I've... had a lot of offers
from other families.

630
00:28:51,313 --> 00:28:55,317
I... just picked you guys,
'cause I liked you the best.

631
00:28:55,359 --> 00:28:57,695
RACHEL:
Oh, damn you, Geller.

632
00:29:01,365 --> 00:29:04,660
Anyway, uh, well, I'm glad
there's no hard feelings.

633
00:29:04,702 --> 00:29:06,078
No, none at all.

634
00:29:06,119 --> 00:29:09,081
You need to be happy
with whoever's in your home.

635
00:29:09,122 --> 00:29:12,376
Although, if you don't mind
telling me...

636
00:29:12,418 --> 00:29:13,419
Hmm?

637
00:29:13,460 --> 00:29:14,836
What was your problem?

638
00:29:14,878 --> 00:29:17,047
Maybe it's something
I can work on in the future.

639
00:29:17,089 --> 00:29:20,718
No... you know, it's-it's,
uh, nothing you did.

640
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:23,387
It's... it's, uh...
it's my issue.

641
00:29:23,429 --> 00:29:26,473
What is it?

642
00:29:26,515 --> 00:29:28,517
( chuckles uncomfortably )

643
00:29:28,559 --> 00:29:30,185
Please?

644
00:29:33,480 --> 00:29:38,026
You know, I'm just not, um...
that comfortable with a guy

645
00:29:38,068 --> 00:29:40,195
who's as sensitive as you.

646
00:29:40,237 --> 00:29:41,238
( sighs )

647
00:29:41,280 --> 00:29:42,322
That's fair.

648
00:29:42,364 --> 00:29:44,700
Although, can I ask...

649
00:29:44,742 --> 00:29:46,952
why do you think that is?

650
00:29:46,993 --> 00:29:49,371
Why? I-I don't know.

651
00:29:53,751 --> 00:29:57,212
Um... uh...

652
00:29:57,254 --> 00:29:59,632
maybe... maybe because
of my father?

653
00:29:59,673 --> 00:30:02,301
Mmm.

654
00:30:02,342 --> 00:30:04,886
I mean, um, you know,
when I was growing up

655
00:30:04,928 --> 00:30:06,555
he was kind of a tough guy.

656
00:30:06,597 --> 00:30:11,435
And as a kid I wasn't
the athlete I am now.

657
00:30:11,477 --> 00:30:13,395
( Rachel guffaws )

658
00:30:13,437 --> 00:30:17,399
I play squash!

659
00:30:19,943 --> 00:30:21,987
Anyway... I, um...

660
00:30:22,028 --> 00:30:25,823
I always got the feeling he
thought I was too sensitive.

661
00:30:25,865 --> 00:30:27,701
That must have been hard.

662
00:30:27,743 --> 00:30:30,912
It was hard.

663
00:30:32,706 --> 00:30:35,584
No, I remember I
was in my bedroom

664
00:30:35,626 --> 00:30:38,337
playing with my dinosaurs--

665
00:30:38,378 --> 00:30:40,172
playing and learning--

666
00:30:42,549 --> 00:30:44,926
and my father walks
in and he says...

667
00:30:44,968 --> 00:30:48,096
he says, "What are you
doing with those things?

668
00:30:48,138 --> 00:30:49,682
"What's wrong with you?

669
00:30:49,723 --> 00:30:51,475
"Why aren't you...

670
00:30:51,517 --> 00:30:54,936
Why aren't you outside playing
like a... like a real boy?"

671
00:30:54,978 --> 00:30:56,689
But you are a real boy.

672
00:30:56,730 --> 00:30:58,398
( crying ):
I know I am.

673
00:31:00,108 --> 00:31:02,569
And when it's summer
and it's hot

674
00:31:02,611 --> 00:31:05,030
why can't you wear a tank top?

675
00:31:06,573 --> 00:31:08,200
It's all right.

676
00:31:08,241 --> 00:31:11,036
Crying is good.

677
00:31:11,077 --> 00:31:14,289
It lets the boo-hoos out.

678
00:31:14,331 --> 00:31:16,875
Here comes some more.

679
00:31:16,916 --> 00:31:21,921
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

680
00:31:25,217 --> 00:31:26,885
And what's the
one kind of boat

681
00:31:26,926 --> 00:31:28,762
that can never ever sink?

682
00:31:28,804 --> 00:31:29,971
What kind?

683
00:31:30,013 --> 00:31:32,808
A friendship.

684
00:31:35,519 --> 00:31:39,147
Wow, you blow my mind.

685
00:31:41,149 --> 00:31:42,108
Oh, I got to go.

686
00:31:42,150 --> 00:31:43,943
Oh... how much
do I owe you?

687
00:31:43,985 --> 00:31:45,195
20 bucks.

688
00:31:45,237 --> 00:31:47,364
Oh, it's like
the cheapest college ever.

